WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.450
Hi! Data can go in a table, or be drawn as a line graph or a pie chart. Today we'll complete a table and learn how to read graphs and answer questions.

2
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:18.810
This table shows how many pupils joined swimming and running. Two boxes are empty.

3
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:24.930
How many swam altogether? 12 boys plus 15 girls is 27.

4
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:34.746
How many boys ran? The total is 30. Take away the 14 girls: 30 minus 14 is 16.

5
00:00:34.896 --> 00:00:42.162
A line graph shows how something changes over time. This is the height of a bean plant over five weeks.

6
00:00:42.312 --> 00:00:49.530
How tall was it in week 4? Go up from week 4 to the point, then look across: 9 cm.

7
00:00:49.680 --> 00:01:02.754
Between which two weeks did it grow most? The steeper the line, the more it grew. From week 2 to week 3 it went from 4 cm to 7 cm, a growth of 3 cm.

8
00:01:02.904 --> 00:01:08.466
A pie chart splits a whole into parts. Here there are 40 pupils in all.

9
00:01:08.616 --> 00:01:16.314
Apples take up half the circle: half of 40 is 20 pupils. Bananas take a quarter: 10 pupils.

10
00:01:16.464 --> 00:01:25.122
Grapes and oranges each take one eighth: 5 pupils each. All the parts add up to exactly 40.

11
00:01:25.272 --> 00:01:32.466
Watch out! Some pupils see 30 and 14 and add them to get 44. That's wrong!

12
00:01:32.616 --> 00:01:38.850
30 is in the Total column. To find one part, subtract the other part from the total.

13
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:45.282
So the number of boys running is 30 minus 14, which is 16.

14
00:01:45.432 --> 00:01:54.906
Your turn! How much did the bean plant grow from week 1 to week 5? Pause and think.

15
00:01:55.056 --> 00:02:04.962
It was 10 cm in week 5 and 2 cm in week 1. 10 minus 2 is 8 cm. Did you get it right?

16
00:02:05.112 --> 00:02:15.522
Another one! In the pie chart, how many more pupils chose bananas than grapes? Pause and think.

17
00:02:15.672 --> 00:02:24.690
Bananas: 10 pupils. Grapes: 5 pupils. That's 5 more. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:34.362
Last one! Between which two weeks did the bean plant grow the least? Pause and think.

19
00:02:34.512 --> 00:02:45.498
Week 4 to week 5: from 9 cm to 10 cm, just 1 cm. The line there is the flattest. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:45.648 --> 00:03:02.754
Remember: with tables and graphs, read the title and units first. In a table, the total is the sum of the parts. On a line graph, a steeper line means a bigger change. In a pie chart, the parts add up to the whole, and you can use fractions to find each part.

21
00:03:02.904 --> 00:03:08.154
Next time you see a chart in the newspaper, try reading it!

